        thing SaveYourSkin's papercut says it cannot express, and it is what separates a glob that
        matches nothing because the work is not done yet (signal) from one that can never match (noise).
        A naive "warn on every zero-match glob" flattens that distinction and will be turned off.

        3. Decide the submodule case explicitly rather than by accident.

        4. Reject a scope path that does not parse as a bare glob.

        One thing this record does NOT claim, because it was checked and is false: the importer is not
        the cause. `akr import` and `akr ingest` set neither `watches` nor `scope` on anything they
        draft — neither string appears in either module. Every dead glob in the census was written by an
        author, not emitted by a tool, which is why the fix has to be a check rather than a generator
        change.
        """
    note """
        LANDED 2026-09-08, with tests: `asserts_its_scope()` replacing the `is_live()` filter so a
        completed record's scope is still checked and a sealed superseded one is not;
        `unverifiable_scopes()` reporting ignored, submodule and project-declared paths as build facts;
        `Repository::run_ls_tree_submodules()` and `inside_submodule()` for the gitlink case; and
        `validate()` in freshness/glob.rs rejecting a glob containing a quote or beginning with the slot
        keyword, with a malformed scope glob now raising AKR-G021 where it used to be skipped in
        silence. AKR-G023's help no longer advertises the copied-prefix case, because AKR-G021 owns it.

        THE BUILD-FACT SHAPE WAS THE DESIGN CALL and a warning would have been wrong. Severity here is
        Error or Warning only and `--strict` is the default, so a new warning would have failed the
        check of every project whose scopes are correct and deliberately outside git. A fact reports
        without failing, which is the shape staleness and scratch already have (D-024, D-036). Two
        corrections followed from reviewing it against real ledgers rather than a sandbox:
        `.agent/scratch/**` is excluded, because AKR manages that directory, `akr scratch keep` invites
        records to cite into it, and `akr check` already reports it on its own line — counting it buried
        the real findings under one workspace's 64 of 78; and the line now names the first four paths
        with their records before falling back to a count, because the staleness fact earns its one line
        by ending in a command to run and this one had none. A fact nobody can act on decays into a
        number people stop reading, which is how these globs accumulated in the first place.

        WHAT THE FIX UNCOVERED, and it is worse than what it was fixing. The new AKR-G021 passed its
        unit test and never reached a user, because `Repository::prime_ignored` was handed every scope
        glob in the ledger before any of them were validated. `git check-ignore -- /abs/path/**` exits
        128 `fatal: Invalid path`, so `unmatched_watches` returned Err, and `session.rs` swallowed it
        with `if let Ok(..)` — discarding every scope and watch diagnostic in the workspace, silently.
        One malformed glob anywhere switched the whole class off. jpegXL-rs has five absolute-path
        scopes pointing into sibling repositories. Both halves are fixed: git is never handed an
        unvalidated glob, and the error is surfaced as an AKR-G001 warning rather than dropped. The
        consequence for this project's own numbers is that any G02x reading taken before this fix,
        including the "clean" workspaces in the 2026-09-08 census, may have been a silence rather than
        an absence.

        NOT CLOSED BY THIS RECORD, and deliberately not overstated. There is still no way for an author
        to say "this path exists and is deliberately untracked"; that is a `project.akr` grammar
        question rather than a matching-predicate one and it is tracked separately. And the
        completed-record change is confirmed but not yet measured at scale: a sweep of four workspaces
        found seven new true positives against a census of 88 occurrences across fifteen, so the
        remaining eleven should be swept before anyone calls the number settled.

        ONE CORRECTION TO AN EARLIER DRAFT OF THIS RECORD. It cited
        saveyourskin.requirement.integration-bridge-jobs/3 as a superseded record carrying an
        unfixable warning. That record is `active`, not superseded, and its dead glob is fixable by
        ordinary revision. The predicate is still right — a sealed record cannot be edited, so warning
        about its scope names a defect with no remedy — but it is right by construction and the example
        was wrong.
        """
    acceptance {
        check completed-records-are-reported {
            statement """
                A completed record's dead scope raises AKR-G023; a superseded record's does not, because a sealed record cannot be edited to fix it.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness a_completed_records_dead_scope_is_still_reported && cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness a_superseded_records_dead_scope_is_not_reported"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.scope-verifiability-suite-20260908/2 ]
        }
        check malformed-globs-say-so {
            statement """
                A scope glob carrying the slot keyword in its value, or a quoted string nested inside another, raises AKR-G021 rather than being silently skipped and later reported as a dead scope.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness a_malformed_scope_glob_is_g021_and_not_a_dead_scope"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.scope-verifiability-suite-20260908/2 ]
        }
        check unverifiable-scopes-are-facts {
            statement """
                A scope path the repository ignores, or one inside a submodule, is reported as a build fact rather than as a diagnostic, and appears in `akr check`'s build-facts block.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness an_ignored_scope_is_a_build_fact_rather_than_a_diagnostic && cargo test -p akr-core --lib submodule"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.scope-verifiability-suite-20260908/2 ]
        }
    }
    supersedes [ @akr.work.a-scope-that-can-never-match/1 ]
}

record akr.work.advisor-packet-handoff/1 : work {
    title "Give AKR a formal worker-to-advisor handoff"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "crates/akr-cli/src/handoff/**",
        path "crates/akr-mcp/src/**",
        path "docs/17-advisor-packets.md",
        path "scripts/agent-section.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Make handing a task to a second model a first-class, addressable AKR operation rather than a hand-written summary. The packet separates administrative fact, which the preparing agent may compress, from worker interpretation, which it may record but not substitute for the problem; the interpretation is withheld until the advisor has reviewed independently, and the reveal is recorded so that independence is knowable afterwards. Delivered as akr handoff create/list/open/expand/reveal/verify/discard, the matching knowledge.handoff_* MCP tools, a workspace fingerprint that reports exact or drifted, and the agent guidance that makes call an advisor mean prepare a packet.
        """
    note """
        Requested with a design brief that identified the failure mode directly: a summary handoff turns the preparing agent into a perceptual bottleneck, so the receiving model must retain independent discovery authority. Recorded as D-040.
        """
    acceptance {
        check blind-read-holds {
            statement """
                akr handoff open and knowledge.handoff_open render the factual layer and leak no worker note; reveal releases them and records that it happened.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-cli --test advisor_packet"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.advisor-packet-suite/1 ]
        }
        check design-set-coherent {
            statement """
                The spec set still coheres with D-040, docs/17 and AKR-C043 in it, and the whole suite passes.
                """
            method command
            command "python tools/check-design.py && cargo test"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.advisor-packet-design-set/1 ]
        }
        check drift-is-reported-not-fatal {
            statement """
                A fresh packet verifies as exact, an edited tree verifies as drifted and names what moved, and neither changes the exit status.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-cli --test advisor_packet a_fresh_packet_is_exact_and_an_edited_tree_drifts"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.advisor-packet-suite/1 ]
        }
        check envelope-stays-project-wide {
            statement """
                A packet's search envelope defaults to the whole project rather than to what the preparing agent examined.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-cli --test advisor_packet the_envelope_defaults_to_the_whole_project"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.advisor-packet-suite/1 ]
        }
        check surfaces-agree {
            statement """
                knowledge.handoff_open and akr handoff open produce an identical result object, and opening over MCP does not stamp the packet.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p akr-mcp --test differential an_advisor_packet"
            verified_by [ @akr.evidence.advisor-packet-suite/1 ]
        }
    }
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record akr.work.advisor-packet-handoff/2 : work {
    title "Give AKR a formal worker-to-advisor handoff"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "crates/akr-cli/src/handoff/**",
        path "crates/akr-mcp/src/**",
        path "docs/17-handoff.md",
